<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Soria</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Soria is a city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> and León, north-central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, capital of the province of the same name on the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/douro">Douro</a>. The province covers the heartland of the ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arevaci">Arevaci</a>, including the ruins of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/numantia">Numantia</a> just north of the city. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> Soria was a Castilian frontier town and a centre of the wool trade, and the poet Antonio Machado lived and taught there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/soria.jpg" alt="Soria" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: FRANCIS RAHER · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Soria_-_P7234619_edited.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
